      "message": "wallet: reject invalid cached xpubs at load\n\nA wallet file whose descriptor cache holds an invalid extended public\nkey aborts the process at load, in an assertion in CPubKey::Derive.\n\nUnserializing such a key leaves it empty. The cache loaders stored the\nempty key. A key is invalid if its public key is not a valid point, or\nif it has depth 0 and a non-zero child number or fingerprint. I return\nDBErrors::CORRUPT for such a record in both caches, as for a record of\nthe wrong size. I tested this with the extended unit test, which fails\nwithout the change and passes with it. A modified wallet file aborted\nbitcoin-wallet before and reports a corrupt wallet now.",
